        "original_id": "f4d3b6e0-8a3b-5ef6-b222-0e27aa45a427",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: 20th Century Fox\n- Works: The Ghost and Mrs. Muir, The Ghost and Mr. Chicken\n- Places: United Kingdom, Century City, Los Angeles, Beverly Hills\n- Topics: film rights, major American film studios\n\nFacts:\n- In 1945, 20th Century Fox bought the film rights to the novel The Ghost and Mrs. Muir, which at that time had been published only in the United Kingdom.\n- In 1947, the film The Ghost and Mrs. Muir was released.\n- 20th Century Fox is one of the \"Big Six\" major American film studios.\n- 20th Century Fox is located in the Century City area of Los Angeles, just west of Beverly Hills.\n- The title of The Ghost and Mr. Chicken is presumably a humorous variation of the film The Ghost and Mrs. Muir.",
